{"slug": "spaghett", "nyt_id": 787062993, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/787062993-spaghett", "name": "Spaghett", "author": "Luke Fortney", "description": "The Spaghett, as it’s known around the world, was invented by Reed Cahill in 2016, when he was a bartender at Wet City Brewing in Baltimore. He’d created beer cocktails before, usually by adding well liquor to a bottle of Lone Star or Coors Banquet. But he altered the course of beverage history when, in a joking riff on an Aperol spritz, he added the Italian aperitif to the so-called Champagne of Beers and named it after a recurring, marinara-stained character on the “Tim and Eric Awesome Show, Great Job!”  The Spaghett does not require a shaker or glassware, though you can build it into a mug or beer can. But the original involves a bottle of Miller High Life, Aperol and lemon.", "servings": {"text": "1 drink", "min": 1, "max": 1, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 5, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 5, "raw": {"total": "5 min", "prep": "PT0H5M", "cook": "PT0H0M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 (12-ounce) bottle light lager (preferably Miller High Life)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "(12-ounce) bottle light lager (preferably miller high life)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ounce Aperol", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "aperol", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ ounce fresh lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Open the beer and pour out (or swig) about 1 ½ ounces"}, {"position": 2, "text": "Pour Aperol directly into the bottle, followed by lemon juice. Serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 172.9, "protein_g": 1.6, "carbohydrates_g": 13.8, "fat_g": 0.0, "saturated_fat_g": 0.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 15.2, "fiber_g": 0.0, "sugar_g": 0.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.0, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["american"], "diet": ["dairy-free", "egg-free", "peanut-free", "tree nut-free", "soy-free", "fish-free", "shellfish-free", "pork-free", "sesame-free", "vegan", "vegetarian", "pescatarian", "low-fat", "low-sodium"], "course": [], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["beer", "lemon juice", "cocktails", "easy", "not-shoppable-ic"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/17/multimedia/17FD-SPAGHETTREX-LF-Spaghett-bgqp/17FD-SPAGHETTREX-LF-Spaghett-bgqp-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 108}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-08-18", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:28:00.888072+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "spanish-chickpea-salad", "nyt_id": 11808, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11808-spanish-chickpea-salad", "name": "Spanish Chickpea Salad", "author": "Robert Farrar Capon", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "6 to 8 servings", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 45, "raw": {"total": "45 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 medium onions, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium onions", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 large cloves garlic, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large cloves garlic", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "⅓ cup extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 1-pound cans chickpeas, drained (liquid reserved)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "1-pound cans chickpeas", "preparation": "drained (liquid reserved)", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 cup canned crushed tomatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "canned crushed tomatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "¼ cup minced parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "minced parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon dried oregano", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "dried oregano", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ teaspoon ground cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ cup prosciutto cut into strips (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "prosciutto cut into strips", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Salt and black pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and black pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a medium-size saucepan over medium heat, simmer the onions and garlic in olive oil until they are soft but not browned. Add the chickpeas, crushed tomatoes, parsley, oregano, cumin and prosciutto, if using, and simmer for 30 minutes more."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Taste the mixture and correct the seasoning with salt and pepper. If it does not seem moist enough, add a little of the reserved chickpea liquid or some olive oil, or both. Serve lukewarm with a green salad and good bread and butter or garlic oil."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 280.7, "protein_g": 11.5, "carbohydrates_g": 31.6, "fat_g": 13.1, "saturated_fat_g": 1.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 6.1, "sodium_mg": 574.5, "fiber_g": 8.6, "sugar_g": 7.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 9.7, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["spanish"], "diet": ["gluten-free", "low-fat"], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["chickpea", "great leftovers", "one pot", "stew"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 64}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1992-10-04", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:50:11.601464+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "spiced-carrot-salad", "nyt_id": 10870, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10870-spiced-carrot-salad", "name": "Spiced Carrot Salad", "author": "Pierre Franey", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "About 20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound fresh carrots (about 12)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh carrots (about 12)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 large garlic clove, peeled but left whole", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large garlic clove", "preparation": "peeled but left whole", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "½ cup fresh lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "⅛ teaspoon cinnamon", "group": null, "quantity": 0.125, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cinnamon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ teaspoon cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ teaspoon paprika", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "paprika", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "⅛ teaspoon cayenne", "group": null, "quantity": 0.125, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cayenne", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "¼ cup olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Chopped parsley for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "chopped parsley for garnish", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Trim and scrape the carrots, and place them in a saucepan."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Cover the carrots with water, and add the garlic and salt. Bring to a boil, and cook for 10 minutes. Drain. Then, cut the carrots into ½-inch rounds (there should be about 2 ½ cups)."}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a bowl, combine the lemon juice, cinnamon, cumin, paprika and cayenne. Blend well. Add the carrots and half the oil. Stir well."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Spoon out individual portions, and sprinkle the remaining oil over them evenly. Garnish with parsley, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 118.1, "protein_g": 0.9, "carbohydrates_g": 9.2, "fat_g": 9.3, "saturated_fat_g": 1.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 249.5, "fiber_g": 2.4, "sugar_g": 4.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 7.7, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "carrot", "easy", "quick", "salad", "vegetables"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 7}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-11-10", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:33:10.447171+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "spicy-cottage-cheese-pasta-alla-vodka", "nyt_id": 786125287, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/786125287-spicy-cottage-cheese-pasta-alla-vodka", "name": "Spicy Cottage Cheese Pasta Alla Vodka", "author": "Tanya Sichynsky", "description": "If you’ve ever wondered if you could swap cottage cheese in for heavy cream in everyone’s favorite fiery pasta sauce — and why wouldn’t you, given cottage cheese’s “It Girl” status — rest assured, you can. It takes a little finesse to ensure the pasta sauce stays luscious, given cottage cheese’s high protein and low fat contents. (This is not the time for low-fat cottage cheese. You need what little fat you can get here, so reach for the whole-milk stuff.) Heed this advice: To keep the sauce from curdling, blitz it for longer than you think it needs, incorporate warm pasta water just a little at a time, and toss it with perfectly cooked, stout rigatoni off heat.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 10, "cook_minutes": 35, "total_minutes": 45, "raw": {"total": "45 min", "prep": "PT0H10M", "cook": "PT0H35M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "4 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil, divided", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": "divided", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 shallots, roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "shallots", "preparation": "roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 garlic cloves, roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 cup (5 ounces) cherry or grape tomatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "(5 ounces) cherry or grape tomatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 (4.5-ounce) tube tomato paste (or a 6-ounce can)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "(4.5-ounce) tube tomato paste (or a 6-ounce can)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon crushed red pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "crushed red pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ cup vodka", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "vodka", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 pound mezze rigatoni or other short tubular pasta", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "mezze rigatoni or other short tubular pasta", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 cup (8 ounces) whole-milk cottage cheese, at room temperature", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "(8 ounces) whole-milk cottage cheese", "preparation": "at room temperature", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 cup (2 ounces) grated Parmesan, more for serving", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "(2 ounces) grated parmesan", "preparation": "more for serving", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "Black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Torn fresh basil leaves, for serving", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "torn fresh basil leaves", "preparation": "for serving", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Set a large pot of generously salted water over high heat to bring to a boil."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, heat 2 tablespoons olive oil in a large, high-sided stainless steel skillet over medium-low. Add the shallot and garlic and cook gently, stirring occasionally, until meltingly soft and just slightly bronzed, 10 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Increase heat to medium and add the cherry tomatoes. Cook, stirring often, until the tomatoes start to slump, wrinkle and burst, 5 to 7 minutes. Gently press on the tomatoes as they soften to encourage their rupturing."}, {"position": 4, "text": "As the tomatoes cook, add the pasta to the boiling water and cook according to package directions for al dente. When it is cooked, reserve 2 cups pasta water, drain the pasta and transfer it back to the pot. Cover to keep warm."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Once the tomatoes are starting to wrinkle and burst, add the tomato paste and crushed red pepper and cook, stirring frequently, until the paste deepens in color like the descending shades of a paint swatch, and the pan is slicked with a terracotta oil, 4 to 5 minutes. Deglaze the pan with vodka, stirring carefully to scrape up any stuck-on bits from the bottom of the pan, and simmer for 1 minute to reduce to a jamlike consistency. Transfer this mixture to the bowl of a food processor and let cool slightly."}, {"position": 6, "text": "To the food processor add the cottage cheese, Parmesan, remaining 2 tablespoons olive oil and a few cracks of black pepper, and blend until smooth — not a chunk in sight! This could take a few minutes, stopping once halfway through to scrape down the sides."}, {"position": 7, "text": "With the processor running, slowly drizzle in 1½ cups of the reserved pasta water, about ½ cup at a time, until well combined and glossy. Taste and adjust seasoning as necessary."}, {"position": 8, "text": "Transfer the sauce to the pot with pasta and toss vigorously off heat, adding a little more pasta water a tablespoon at a time — you don’t want the sauce to curdle — to loosen it up if desired. Serve topped with more black pepper and Parmesan, and garnish with torn basil."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 775.3, "protein_g": 28.8, "carbohydrates_g": 100.8, "fat_g": 21.6, "saturated_fat_g": 5.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 19.3, "sodium_mg": 757.0, "fiber_g": 6.7, "sugar_g": 11.8, "unsaturated_fat_g": 14.0, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian american inspired"], "diet": ["egg-free", "peanut-free", "tree nut-free", "soy-free", "fish-free", "shellfish-free", "pork-free", "sesame-free", "vegetarian", "pescatarian", "high fiber"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["cottage cheese", "vodka", "rigatoni", "tomato paste", "red pepper flake", "parmesan", "pastas", "food processor", "stovetop", "easy", "quick", "weeknight", "cherry tomato", "grape tomato", "the veggie"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/07/multimedia/TS-Cottage-Cheese-Pasta-Alla-Vodka-1zfvw/TS-Cottage-Cheese-Pasta-Alla-Vodka-zfvw-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 461}, "video_url": "https://www.nytimes.com/video/embedded/dining/100000011088533/spicy-cottage-cheese-pasta-alla-vodka.html", "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-08-12", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:27:37.087850+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "spicy-stir-fried-tofu-with-kale-and-red-pepper", "nyt_id": 12277, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12277-spicy-stir-fried-tofu-with-kale-and-red-pepper", "name": "Spicy Stir-Fried Tofu With Kale and Red Pepper", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "Kale is a member of the cruciferous family of vegetables (genus Brassica), so named because their flowers have four petals in the shape of a cross. A nutritional powerhouse that tastes wonderful when properly cooked, kale is one of nature’s best sources of vitamins A, C and K and a very good source of copper, potassium, iron, manganese and phosphorus. These greens are hearty, and they maintain about 50 percent of their volume when you cook them, unlike spinach, which cooks down to a fraction of its volume. The various types of kale also maintain a lot of texture, which makes them perfect for stir-fries.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 bunch curly kale (about 10 ounces), stemmed and washed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "bunch", "item": "curly kale (about 10 ounces)", "preparation": "stemmed and washed", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 14-ounce package firm tofu, sliced about ¼ inch thick", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "14-ounce package firm tofu", "preparation": "sliced about ¼ inch thick", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 tablespoon soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon Shao Hsing rice wine or dry sherry", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "shao hsing rice wine or dry sherry", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "¼ cup chicken or vegetable stock", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chicken or vegetable stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon cornstarch", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cornstarch", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¼ teaspoon salt (more to taste)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt (more to taste)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¼ to ½ teaspoon ground pepper, preferably white pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground pepper", "preparation": "preferably white pepper", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "¼ teaspoon sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 tablespoon peanut oil or canola oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "peanut oil or canola oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 tablespoon minced garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 tablespoon minced ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 serrano pepper, seeded and minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "serrano pepper", "preparation": "seeded and minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 red bell pepper, cut in 2-inch julienne", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "red bell pepper", "preparation": "cut in 2-inch julienne", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "2 teaspoons dark sesame oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "dark sesame oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring a medium saucepan of lightly salted water to a boil, add the kale and blanch 1 minute. Transfer to a bowl of cold water, drain and squeeze out excess water. Chop coarsely and place in a bowl near your wok."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Cut the tofu into dominos and place them on paper towels. Place another paper towel on top and prepare the remaining ingredients."}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a small bowl or measuring cup, combine the soy sauce, rice wine or sherry, stock and cornstarch. Combine the salt, pepper and sugar in another small bowl. Have all the ingredients within arm’s length of your wok."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Heat a 14-inch flat-bottomed wok or 12-inch steel skillet over high heat until a drop of water evaporates within a second or two when added to the pan. Swirl in the canola or peanut oil by adding it to the sides of the pan and swirling the pan, then add the tofu. Stir-fry 1 to 2 minutes, until it begins to color. Add the garlic, ginger and chili and stir-fry for no more than 10 seconds."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Add the red pepper and stir-fry for 1 minute. Add the kale, salt, pepper and sugar and toss together. Add the soy sauce mixture and the sesame oil. Stir-fry for another 30 seconds to a minute. Remove from the heat and serve with grains or noodles."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 246.6, "protein_g": 20.5, "carbohydrates_g": 10.7, "fat_g": 15.7, "saturated_fat_g": 2.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.4, "sodium_mg": 440.0, "fiber_g": 6.0, "sugar_g": 2.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 12.0, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["dairy-free", "healthy", "vegan", "vegetarian"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["kale", "low cholesterol", "red bell pepper", "stir-fry", "tofu", "weeknight", "winter"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2012/01/31/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "Spicy Stir-Fried Tofu With Kale and Red Pepper", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 421}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2012-01-30", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:54:48.936260+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
